WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.563 --> 00:00:01.631
are investigating.

00:00:01.698 --> 00:00:02.866
We don't know why this is just

00:00:02.999 --> 00:00:03.633
coming to light today.

00:00:03.766 --> 00:00:04.200
&gt;&gt; All right.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.635
Gabe Cohen, thank you so much.

00:00:05.735 --> 00:00:06.069
Appreciate it.

00:00:06.202 --> 00:00:07.904
&gt;&gt;&gt; With us now, Republican

00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:09.672
senator Dan Sullivan of Alaska.

00:00:09.806 --> 00:00:11.641
He's a Marine Corps veteran,

00:00:11.741 --> 00:00:12.976
member of the reserves who

00:00:13.109 --> 00:00:14.277
serves on the senate commerce

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.945
and armed services committee and

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:16.813
participated in today's hearing.

00:00:16.946 --> 00:00:18.147
Thanks for joining us.

00:00:18.281 --> 00:00:19.649
&gt;&gt; Thanks for having me.

00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:21.651
&gt;&gt; Are you confident a

00:00:21.784 --> 00:00:22.652
catastrophic meltdown like what

00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:23.920
happened last month will not

00:00:24.053 --> 00:00:24.454
happen again?

00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:26.589
&gt;&gt; No, I'm not confident.

00:00:26.723 --> 00:00:28.358
That's why we held a hearing.

00:00:28.491 --> 00:00:29.659
Actually, this is the second

00:00:29.659 --> 00:00:30.760
hearing we've held on aviation

00:00:30.894 --> 00:00:32.262
safety and issues just in the

00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:34.931
last two weeks on the commerce

00:00:35.064 --> 00:00:35.298
committee.

00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:36.532
You might remember the southwest

00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:40.103
meltdown over the holidays.

00:00:40.236 --> 00:00:41.237
Then the notam meltdown.

00:00:41.671 --> 00:00:42.572
This is a big wake-up call for

00:00:42.705 --> 00:00:45.108
our country and certainly the

00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:47.677
FAA, and it's this -- it's old

00:00:47.677 --> 00:00:47.777
technology.

00:00:47.911 --> 00:00:50.046
We need to update technology to

00:00:50.179 --> 00:00:51.681
make sure our systems are able

00:00:51.714 --> 00:00:53.683
to function well, function

00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.352
during storms like we saw over

00:00:56.486 --> 00:00:59.689
the holidays, and make sure we

00:00:59.689 --> 00:01:01.991
continue to have the safest

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:02.725
aviation travel system anywhere

00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:07.697
in the world.

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:08.364
&gt;&gt; Is there appetite on capitol

00:01:08.498 --> 00:01:09.332
hill to spend the money to

00:01:09.699 --> 00:01:11.334
update the technology so that we

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:16.272
have the systems we need?

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:18.408
&gt;&gt; Oh, I think absolutely,

00:01:18.541 --> 00:01:19.709
certainly from this senator you

00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:19.809
do.

00:01:19.943 --> 00:01:20.777
And here's the reason, Jake.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.713
I mean, Americans take for

00:01:23.713 --> 00:01:24.847
granted that we have, like I

00:01:24.981 --> 00:01:26.883
said, the safest air travel of

00:01:27.016 --> 00:01:28.351
anyplace on the planet.

00:01:28.484 --> 00:01:29.719
It's a great record.

00:01:29.752 --> 00:01:31.955
But what we don't want, and

00:01:32.088 --> 00:01:33.723
we're starting to see

00:01:33.723 --> 00:01:34.657
indications that it could

00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:38.227
happen, we don't want

00:01:38.361 --> 00:01:39.729
innovations and technological

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:40.730
advancements spurred by some

00:01:40.863 --> 00:01:42.432
kind of major disaster.

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:43.933
We want to be able to be in

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:44.667
front of this.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:47.737
To me, the signals are out there

00:01:47.737 --> 00:01:49.739
already that we need to be

00:01:49.772 --> 00:01:51.107
proactive, not reactive.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.242
And I'll tell you this, in my

00:01:53.376 --> 00:01:54.777
state, in the great state of

00:01:54.911 --> 00:01:56.546
Alaska, boy, we need huge

00:01:56.679 --> 00:01:58.881
upgrades to our aviation system.

00:01:59.015 --> 00:02:00.416
We have over 250 communities

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.819
that aren't connected by roads,

00:02:02.952 --> 00:02:06.189
and you need safe travel by air

00:02:06.322 --> 00:02:08.057
in Alaska but across the

00:02:08.191 --> 00:02:08.391
country.

00:02:08.524 --> 00:02:09.125
So the answer to your question

00:02:09.258 --> 00:02:11.194
is absolutely yes.

00:02:11.327 --> 00:02:13.763
&gt;&gt; And now we're talking about

00:02:13.863 --> 00:02:15.765
three near collisions involving

00:02:15.765 --> 00:02:16.666
huge passenger planes.

00:02:16.799 --> 00:02:18.167
There was one we just learned

00:02:18.301 --> 00:02:19.769
about in Honolulu.

00:02:19.802 --> 00:02:21.204
All of these were within a month

00:02:21.337 --> 00:02:21.838
of each other.

00:02:21.971 --> 00:02:23.773
Did you get answers on how this

00:02:23.773 --> 00:02:25.375
is being addressed?

00:02:25.775 --> 00:02:27.176
&gt;&gt; Well, to be honest, the news

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.779
of the third one is something

00:02:29.812 --> 00:02:31.781
that I just learned about as

00:02:31.848 --> 00:02:32.015
well.

00:02:32.148 --> 00:02:34.217
But it makes the point that I've

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.785
been making, which is we need to

00:02:35.852 --> 00:02:38.154
get in front of this.

00:02:38.287 --> 00:02:40.089
Three warnings, three warnings,

00:02:40.223 --> 00:02:41.791
and in addition, like I said, to

00:02:41.791 --> 00:02:43.326
the meltdown of southwest over

00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:45.795
the holidays, to me is a very

00:02:45.795 --> 00:02:46.662
significant warning that we've

00:02:46.796 --> 00:02:49.799
got to take preemptive measures,

00:02:49.799 --> 00:02:51.200
proactive measures to make sure

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.001
we have safety.

00:02:52.135 --> 00:02:53.236
That's why we've had two

00:02:53.369 --> 00:02:54.971
hearings in the last two weeks

00:02:55.104 --> 00:02:55.805
on this.

00:02:55.805 --> 00:02:56.639
We'll continue to do it.

00:02:56.773 --> 00:02:59.042
We also need an FAA

00:02:59.175 --> 00:02:59.475
administrator.

00:02:59.809 --> 00:03:02.078
You saw today the witness was an

00:03:02.211 --> 00:03:03.112
acting administrator.

00:03:03.246 --> 00:03:06.382
We need a full senate-confirmed

00:03:06.516 --> 00:03:07.917
administrator soon, have the

00:03:08.051 --> 00:03:09.819
hearings soon to press on these

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:11.154
issues when he goes through his

00:03:11.287 --> 00:03:11.821
confirmation.

00:03:11.821 --> 00:03:13.456
&gt;&gt; Let's urn to another issue I

00:03:13.823 --> 00:03:15.825
know is important to you as an

00:03:15.825 --> 00:03:16.025
alaskan.

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:16.726
The Chinese spy balloon.

00:03:16.859 --> 00:03:17.260
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:03:17.393 --> 00:03:20.196
&gt;&gt; The senate got a classified

00:03:20.329 --> 00:03:20.897
briefing on China in the last

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:21.264
hour.

00:03:21.397 --> 00:03:22.632
Do you think president Biden

00:03:22.765 --> 00:03:24.467
handled this correctly, both the

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.437
spy balloon and also the three

00:03:27.837 --> 00:03:28.771
subsequent aircraft -- had that

00:03:28.905 --> 00:03:29.472
have been shot down from the

00:03:29.839 --> 00:03:32.408
sky?

00:03:32.542 --> 00:03:33.976
&gt;&gt; The first thing you mentioned

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:34.710
in Alaska.

00:03:34.844 --> 00:03:36.179
The first thing I want to do is

00:03:36.412 --> 00:03:39.982
a shout-out to the Alaska air

00:03:40.116 --> 00:03:40.583
forces, National Guard.

00:03:40.716 --> 00:03:41.851
Think about what they've done in

00:03:41.851 --> 00:03:42.652
the last ten days.

00:03:42.785 --> 00:03:44.454
They tracked this big balloon.

00:03:44.587 --> 00:03:46.556
They went and intercepted it.

00:03:46.689 --> 00:03:49.492
They tracked these smaller radar

00:03:49.859 --> 00:03:52.061
signatures of objects.

00:03:52.195 --> 00:03:52.795
They went and intercepted those,

00:03:52.929 --> 00:03:54.430
shot two of those down, the one

00:03:54.564 --> 00:03:56.432
over Alaska, the one over

00:03:56.566 --> 00:03:56.766
Canada.

00:03:56.899 --> 00:04:00.236
Those were alaskan base forces

00:04:00.369 --> 00:04:03.072
that shot the Canadian one.

00:04:03.206 --> 00:04:03.873
And just yesterday they

00:04:03.973 --> 00:04:04.740
intercepted a bear bomb we are

00:04:04.874 --> 00:04:06.142
two fighter escorts that was

00:04:06.275 --> 00:04:10.713
trying to get into Alaska.

00:04:10.847 --> 00:04:12.148
That was wo weeks of work.

00:04:12.281 --> 00:04:13.483
Our military forces in ak ank,

00:04:13.883 --> 00:04:15.918
which by the way is the top

00:04:16.052 --> 00:04:17.386
cover of America, were so

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.455
critical to our nation's

00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:21.190
defenses, they've been working

00:04:21.324 --> 00:04:21.557
overtime.

00:04:21.891 --> 00:04:23.459
But I will tell you this.

00:04:23.893 --> 00:04:24.694
I've been satisfied with the

00:04:24.827 --> 00:04:27.263
briefings I've gotten from the

00:04:27.396 --> 00:04:28.431
military.

00:04:28.564 --> 00:04:32.301
General van hurt, the north com

00:04:32.435 --> 00:04:33.102
commander, has kept me well

00:04:33.236 --> 00:04:34.203
informed on the tracking of the

00:04:34.337 --> 00:04:34.837
object Friday.

00:04:35.004 --> 00:04:36.372
I strongly encouraged him, by

00:04:36.506 --> 00:04:38.941
the way, in a bipartisan manner,

00:04:39.075 --> 00:04:40.576
to shoot that aircraft down,

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:41.944
which is what they ended up

00:04:42.078 --> 00:04:42.245
doing.

00:04:42.378 --> 00:04:43.913
But where I have not been

00:04:43.913 --> 00:04:45.014
satisfied is the broader

00:04:45.148 --> 00:04:46.849
administration's lack of

00:04:46.983 --> 00:04:47.283
transparency.

00:04:47.416 --> 00:04:48.584
There are a number of things we

00:04:48.718 --> 00:04:51.120
learned in the briefing

00:04:51.254 --> 00:04:53.523
yesterday that I've been aware

00:04:53.923 --> 00:04:54.757
of that I think the American

00:04:54.891 --> 00:04:56.292
people should know about.

00:04:56.425 --> 00:04:57.426
And, you know, there's things

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.661
that they should let us know.

00:04:58.794 --> 00:04:59.929
There's things they should tell

00:04:59.929 --> 00:05:00.630
us they don't know.

00:05:00.763 --> 00:05:02.265
Of course they shouldn't let on

00:05:02.398 --> 00:05:03.933
to sources and methods.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.935
But I don't think they've been

00:05:06.002 --> 00:05:06.402
transparent enough.

00:05:06.536 --> 00:05:09.305
As you know, when they're not

00:05:09.438 --> 00:05:10.806
transparent, then, you know, the

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.775
wild speculation, unfounded

00:05:12.909 --> 00:05:13.943
fears can result in the public.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.478
They need to be more

00:05:15.611 --> 00:05:15.945
transparent.

00:05:16.012 --> 00:05:16.579
&gt;&gt; Anything you want to share

00:05:16.712 --> 00:05:18.014
with us from the briefing?

00:05:18.147 --> 00:05:19.382
I'm sure our viewers would love

00:05:19.515 --> 00:05:19.949
to hear.

00:05:20.016 --> 00:05:22.118
&gt;&gt; Well, look, today's briefing

00:05:22.251 --> 00:05:23.119
was actually -- yesterday's

00:05:23.252 --> 00:05:24.287
briefing was on the balloons.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.123
And I pressed them to share

00:05:27.256 --> 00:05:28.925
more, which I think is V its up

00:05:29.058 --> 00:05:31.961
to the executive branch to do.

00:05:31.961 --> 00:05:33.629
Today's briefing was on the

00:05:33.963 --> 00:05:35.264
broader China threat.

00:05:35.398 --> 00:05:36.666
It was the assessment.

00:05:36.799 --> 00:05:37.967
It's still going on.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.435
It's a highly classified

00:05:39.569 --> 00:05:40.937
briefing, but I will tell you

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.371
this, it was a sobering

00:05:42.505 --> 00:05:43.506
briefing, because our military

00:05:43.639 --> 00:05:44.974
advantage relative to the

00:05:45.107 --> 00:05:47.043
Chinese continues to erode.

00:05:47.176 --> 00:05:49.979
And we need to focus on that,

00:05:50.046 --> 00:05:50.947
and I'm calling on the president

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.015
to focus on that.

00:05:53.149 --> 00:05:53.983
It was his administration giving

00:05:54.016 --> 00:05:55.985
this briefing that I just walked

00:05:55.985 --> 00:05:57.486
out of about the erosion of our

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.989
advantage relative to the

00:06:00.056 --> 00:06:00.323
Chinese.

00:06:00.456 --> 00:06:01.257
And each year the president

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:05.094
sends up a budget for defense

00:06:05.228 --> 00:06:06.429
that's defense cuts.

00:06:06.562 --> 00:06:09.999
And, you know, it's a huge

00:06:09.999 --> 00:06:10.266
disconnect.

00:06:10.399 --> 00:06:12.001
His administration is literally

00:06:12.001 --> 00:06:13.102
telling 100 senators right now

00:06:13.236 --> 00:06:14.804
about the challenges and the

00:06:14.937 --> 00:06:16.005
erosion of our military

00:06:16.105 --> 00:06:17.073
advantage, and each year they

00:06:17.206 --> 00:06:19.575
send up cuts to the Pentagon.

00:06:20.009 --> 00:06:20.142
Makes no sense.

00:06:20.276 --> 00:06:22.311
And I think they need to put

00:06:22.445 --> 00:06:25.281
forward a budget that reflects

00:06:25.414 --> 00:06:26.315
the threats that they're

00:06:26.449 --> 00:06:27.316
briefing senators on right now.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.085
&gt;&gt; Also, U.S. Intelligence

00:06:29.218 --> 00:06:31.520
officials are investigating the

00:06:31.654 --> 00:06:32.955
possibility that that Chinese

00:06:33.089 --> 00:06:34.490
spy balloon was meant to fly

00:06:34.624 --> 00:06:36.025
over Guam, where the U.S. Has

00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:38.094
military facilities, but instead

00:06:38.227 --> 00:06:40.296
was blown wildly off course

00:06:40.429 --> 00:06:44.433
because of strong winds.

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:45.067
What do you make of that?

00:06:45.201 --> 00:06:46.335
&gt;&gt; So, again, this is what's a

00:06:46.469 --> 00:06:47.570
little frustrating.

00:06:47.703 --> 00:06:49.372
I've been in several classified

00:06:49.505 --> 00:06:52.041
briefings about these spy

00:06:52.041 --> 00:06:52.208
balloons.

00:06:52.341 --> 00:06:52.942
I have not heard that in any of

00:06:53.075 --> 00:06:54.076
the classified briefings.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.679
We had briefings yesterday that

00:06:56.812 --> 00:06:59.148
said in a classified setting

00:06:59.282 --> 00:07:03.252
that the Pentagon and the

00:07:03.386 --> 00:07:04.053
intelligence community was not

00:07:04.153 --> 00:07:05.421
sure where these additional

00:07:05.554 --> 00:07:08.057
balloons and Octobers have come

00:07:08.157 --> 00:07:08.391
from.

00:07:09.158 --> 00:07:10.760
I still think we should suspect

00:07:10.893 --> 00:07:14.063
the worst, like our adversaries,

00:07:14.196 --> 00:07:14.964
China and Russia.

00:07:15.097 --> 00:07:16.432
And then you have right after

00:07:16.565 --> 00:07:18.868
that briefing admiral Kirby at

00:07:19.001 --> 00:07:20.069
the national security council

00:07:20.169 --> 00:07:20.970
staff saying he doesn't think

00:07:21.103 --> 00:07:23.105
it's China at all.

00:07:23.239 --> 00:07:24.707
Again, that's a disconnect to

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.242
what 100 senators were told

00:07:26.375 --> 00:07:27.310
yesterday, so I think they need

00:07:27.443 --> 00:07:28.377
to get their story straight.

00:07:28.511 --> 00:07:31.614
My understanding of that Chinese

00:07:31.747 --> 00:07:33.416
spy balloon had propulsion to do

00:07:33.549 --> 00:07:35.084
some directional travel, so I'm

00:07:35.217 --> 00:07:37.653
not sure it was subject fully to

00:07:38.087 --> 00:07:40.256
the winds, and it seemed to be

00:07:40.389 --> 00:07:41.090
directed over Alaska and the

00:07:41.223 --> 00:07:42.992
rest of the country in a way

00:07:43.125 --> 00:07:44.093
that was purposeful.

